      "title": "Your head is older than your feet",
      "status": "in review",
      "youtube": {
        "title": "Your head is older than your feet",
        "description": "Your head ticks a tiny bit faster than your feet. Gravity slows time, so the higher you are, the faster your time runs.\n\nIn 2010, physicists at NIST, a U.S. lab, raised an atomic clock by about a foot (two steps up a staircase). The higher clock ticked faster. Over a 79-year life, that adds up to about 90 billionths of a second. GPS satellite clocks run fast too, so engineers set them slower before launch.\n\nCase file 001: TRUE. The higher you are, the faster your time runs.\n\nSource: NIST news release, 23 Sept 2010.\n\n#Shorts #Science #Physics #Relativity #UnrealActually"
      },
